{"relationshipsSections":[{"title":"Conforms To","type":"conformsTo","kind":"relationships","identifiers":["doc:\/\/GraphProtocols\/documentation\/GraphProtocols\/Graph","doc:\/\/GraphProtocols\/documentation\/GraphProtocols\/MutableGraph","doc:\/\/GraphProtocols\/documentation\/GraphProtocols\/PropertyGraph","doc:\/\/AdjacencyListModule\/s8CopyableP","doc:\/\/AdjacencyListModule\/s28CustomDebugStringConvertibleP","doc:\/\/AdjacencyListModule\/s17CustomReflectableP","doc:\/\/AdjacencyListModule\/s23CustomStringConvertibleP","doc:\/\/AdjacencyListModule\/Se","doc:\/\/AdjacencyListModule\/SE","doc:\/\/AdjacencyListModule\/SQ","doc:\/\/AdjacencyListModule\/s9EscapableP","doc:\/\/AdjacencyListModule\/s30ExpressibleByDictionaryLiteralP","doc:\/\/AdjacencyListModule\/SH","doc:\/\/AdjacencyListModule\/s8SendableP","doc:\/\/AdjacencyListModule\/s16SendableMetatypeP"]}],"schemaVersion":{"minor":3,"patch":0,"major":0},"sections":[],"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"An undirected graph stored as adjacency lists, the undirected counterpart of "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"AdjacencyList"},{"type":"text","text":"."}],"metadata":{"role":"symbol","roleHeading":"Structure","remoteSource":{"url":"https:\/\/github.com\/Tyler-Keith-Thompson\/Grafluent\/blob\/main\/Sources\/AdjacencyListModule\/UndirectedAdjacencyList.swift#L26","fileName":"UndirectedAdjacencyList.swift"},"fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"struct"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"UndirectedAdjacencyList"}],"symbolKind":"struct","modules":[{"name":"AdjacencyListModule"}],"title":"UndirectedAdjacencyList","externalID":"s:19AdjacencyListModule010UndirectedaB0V","navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"UndirectedAdjacencyList"}]},"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/AdjacencyListModule\/documentation\/AdjacencyListModule"]]},"primaryContentSections":[{"declarations":[{"tokens":[{"text":"@frozen","kind":"attribute"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"struct","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"UndirectedAdjacencyList","kind":"identifier"},{"text":"<","kind":"text"},{"text":"Vertex","kind":"genericParameter"},{"text":"> ","kind":"text"},{"text":"where","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Vertex","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":" : ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Hashable","preciseIdentifier":"s:SH","kind":"typeIdentifier"}],"platforms":["Linux"],"languages":["swift"]}],"kind":"declarations"},{"content":[{"text":"Overview","level":2,"anchor":"overview","type":"heading"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"The vertex set is any set of ","type":"text"},{"code":"Hashable","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" values. The edge set is a set of unordered pairs of","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"vertices. Self-loops are allowed, parallel edges are not, and ","type":"text"},{"code":"{u, v}","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" is the same edge as","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"code":"{v, u}","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":".","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Vertices are kept in dense slots, with a dictionary from vertex to slot. While the vertices are"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"the "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Int"},{"type":"text","text":"s "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"0..<n"},{"type":"text","text":" in order, each is its own slot and there is no dictionary. Edges are kept in"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"an array, so an edge’s position in "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"edges"},{"type":"text","text":" is an "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Int"},{"type":"text","text":" in "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"0..<edgeCount"},{"type":"text","text":". Each slot has a row"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"of the slots of its neighbors and a parallel row of the positions of its incident edges. Each"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"edge is in both its endpoints’ rows, and a self-loop is in its vertex’s row twice. The rows"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"share one array per kind, so the graph makes a constant number of allocations however many"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"vertices it has. The bulk initializers ("},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"init(vertices:edges:)"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"init(edges:)"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"init(_:)"},{"type":"text","text":","},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"init(adjacency:)"},{"type":"text","text":", the builder and the dictionary literal) lay every row out once at its exact"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"size, in slot order; a row that later outgrows its block moves to the end. A hash table from unordered slot pair to position answers "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"contains(edge:)"},{"type":"text","text":" in"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"O(1) expected."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Removing an edge is O(1). The last edge moves into its position, and the last entry of each row"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"into the hole. Removing a vertex costs O(degree) and moves the last slot into its place. Vertex"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"order, edge order and edge positions are therefore unspecified and may change after a removal."},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"Maps attached to the graph ("},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"addEdgeMap(default:)"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"PropertyGraph"},{"type":"text","text":") move their values with"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"them. Each edge keeps the orientation it was first inserted with."}],"type":"paragraph"}],"kind":"content"}],"kind":"symbol","variants":[{"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}],"paths":["\/documentation\/adjacencylistmodule\/undirectedadjacencylist"]}],"topicSections":[{"title":"Initializers","anchor":"Initializers","identifiers":["doc:\/\/AdjacencyListModule\/documentation\/AdjacencyListModule\/UndirectedAdjacencyList\/init()","doc:\/\/AdjacencyListModule\/documentation\/AdjacencyListModule\/UndirectedAdjacencyList\/init(_:)-17f2v","doc:\/\/AdjacencyListModule\/documentation\/AdjacencyListModule\/UndirectedAdjacencyList\/init(_:)-2o9bq","doc:\/\/AdjacencyListModule\/documentation\/AdjacencyListModule\/UndirectedAdjacencyList\/init(adjacency:)","doc:\/\/AdjacencyListModule\/documentation\/AdjacencyListModule\/UndirectedAdjacencyList\/init(edges:)","doc:\/\/AdjacencyListModule\/documentation\/AdjacencyListModule\/UndirectedAdjacencyList\/init(vertices:)","doc:\/\/AdjacencyListModule\/documentation\/AdjacencyListModule\/UndirectedAdjacencyList\/init(vertices:edges:)"],"generated":true},{"title":"Instance Methods","anchor":"Instance-Methods","identifiers":["doc:\/\/AdjacencyListModule\/documentation\/AdjacencyListModule\/UndirectedAdjacencyList\/degree(checked:)","doc:\/\/AdjacencyListModule\/documentation\/AdjacencyListModule\/UndirectedAdjacencyList\/edges(between:and:)","doc:\/\/AdjacencyListModule\/documentation\/AdjacencyListModule\/UndirectedAdjacencyList\/incidentEdges(checked:)","doc:\/\/AdjacencyListModule\/documentation\/AdjacencyListModule\/UndirectedAdjacencyList\/insert(checked:)","doc:\/\/AdjacencyListModule\/documentation\/AdjacencyListModule\/UndirectedAdjacencyList\/insert(edge:)","doc:\/\/AdjacencyListModule\/documentation\/AdjacencyListModule\/UndirectedAdjacencyList\/neighbors(checked:)","doc:\/\/AdjacencyListModule\/documentation\/AdjacencyListModule\/UndirectedAdjacencyList\/vertexIndex(checked:)"],"generated":true},{"title":"Type Aliases","anchor":"Type-Aliases","identifiers":["doc:\/\/AdjacencyListModule\/documentation\/AdjacencyListModule\/UndirectedAdjacencyList\/EdgesConnecting"],"generated":true},{"title":"Default Implementations","anchor":"Default-Implementations","identifiers":["doc:\/\/AdjacencyList